    "description": "Delly is an integrated structural variant (SV) and copy-number variant (CNV) prediction method that can discover, genotype and visualize deletions, insertions, tandem duplications, inversions and translocations at single-nucleotide resolution in short-read and long-read whole-genome sequencing data. It uses paired-ends, split-reads and read-depth to discover and genotype SVs in the genome.",
